        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-3)^2+y^2=16$",
          "worked": "Using $(x-h)^2+(y-k)^2=r^2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(x-3)^2+(y-0)^2&=4^2\\\\(x-3)^2+y^2&=16\\end{align*}$$",
